1
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,480
Dear listeners.

2
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:11,680
Today is

3
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:12,810
October 23rd, 2010.

4
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:14,520
The closely watched Typhoon Megi

5
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,920
swept across Luzon Island
in the Philippines a week ago

6
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:19,050
and is heading straight for Checheng.

7
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:21,160
Although its intensity
has significantly weakened,

8
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,680
it will still bring fierce winds
and heavy rain.

9
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:26,010
Please keep your doors and windows closed

10
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,300
and take precautions.

11
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:33,800
Captain Li,

12
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,730
facing the power of nature,

13
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:37,520
you should compose a poem.

14
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,579
We've already been
to nine accident scenes.

15
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,120
Aren't you tired?

16
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,460
Captain Li,

17
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,120
I may be a rookie,

18
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,760
but I've heard from Sister Li
and the others.

19
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:49,240
You used to be in the literary circle.

20
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,900
I even read your poems online.

21
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,200
I'm not flattering you,

22
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:53,880
but you're a well-deserved poet.

23
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,440
Poet?

24
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:57,960
We are pretty wet.

25
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:59,400
This damn rain.

26
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:01,010
I hope it stops soon.

27
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:02,760
Two are already dead.

28
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:04,500
We can't have any more.

29
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:05,880
Captain Li,

30
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,680
have you heard of

31
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,200
Murphy's Law?

32
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:11,580
Speak English.

33
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:12,680
It means

34
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:15,340
whatever can go wrong, will go wrong.

35
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,560
Pfft, pfft, pfft.

36
00:03:17,079 --> 00:03:17,840
Let me tell you,

37
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,320
you've only been
on the force for two days,

38
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:20,920
and I already know your nickname.

39
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:21,960
Jinx, right?

40
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,160
Pfft, pfft, pfft.

41
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:36,579
Li Xingchen, Traffic Accident Brigade.

42
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,320
Understood. Copy that.

43
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,770
I'll be right there.

44
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,000
Your mouth

45
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,850
really lives up to its reputation.

46
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,000
Go drive.

47
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,720
Okay, okay.

48
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:09,040
The mountain road behind the power plant
is really tough to drive on.

49
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,120
There was an accident
at the intersection too.

50
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,360
Alright, alright.

51
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:13,640
We're here.

52
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,920
You're finally here.

53
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,160
Next is...

54
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,080
you.

55
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,690
You know each other?

56
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:34,960
No,

57
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,560
did I s-say

58
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:37,840
something wrong?

59
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,000
Officer Li,

60
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,200
you're really a nice guy.

61
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,440
Too bad

62
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:44,120
we're not a match.

63
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:47,640
I understand.

64
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:51,680
I hope your next relationship is better

65
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:53,120
than the last.

66
00:04:54,159 --> 00:04:54,920
Thank you.

67
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:56,560
Captain Li,

68
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:58,180
Captain Li!

69
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,850
You know each other?

70
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:02,320
Ms. Shen,

71
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,720
where is the victim?

72
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,980
What's the situation?

73
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:07,360
S-Sitting over there.

74
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:08,600
But

75
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,600
he's already dead.

76
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,120
Already dead?

77
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,600
And he's still sitting?

78
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,000
How do you know he's dead?

79
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:19,660
The police officer
who left earlier said so.

80
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,480
Left earlier?

81
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:25,080
You mean someone was here before us?

82
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,080
Right after the crash,

83
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,040
a traffic cop showed up.

84
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:35,640
He said the person was already dead.

85
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:45,640
I'm a traffic cop.

86
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,970
Had an accident, right?

87
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,040
Traffic cop?

88
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,780
But I haven't even called the police yet.

89
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:57,320
I'm on duty.

90
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:58,409
Just passing by.

91
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,610
What should I do now?

92
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:03,880
I just checked.

93
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,260
The person is dead.

94
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,920
Let's clear the scene first.

95
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:09,720
Clear

96
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:12,400
the scene?

97
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,600
Pull your car over first.

98
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,000
Don't block the traffic.

99
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,260
His neck is broken.

100
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:27,880
Jiang,

101
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,680
call an ambulance first.

102
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,800
Are you saying

103
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,600
that guy touched the body?

104
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,960
I thought it was weird too.

105
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,520
Normally,

106
00:06:48,840 --> 00:06:51,159
shouldn't you inspect the scene first?

107
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,280
That's how it is on TV shows.

108
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:57,040
Did he show you his badge?

109
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:59,080
No.

110
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,480
He said he was a traffic cop

111
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:02,040
and was wearing the uniform.

112
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,440
And he drove a police car,

113
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,480
so I didn't ask.

114
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:05,360
Jiang,

115
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,120
go verify this.

116
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,440
See if another unit was passing by

117
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,240
and responded.

118
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:09,970
Understood.

119
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,530
Tell me about the crash.

120
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:16,330
Be as detailed as possible.

121
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,560
I was passing by,

122
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,480
and it was raining heavily.

123
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,400
And I was playing music in my car.

124
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:23,770
The rhythm might

125
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,040
have been a bit fast.

126
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:26,680
And it was quite loud.

127
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:26,920
And it was quite loud.

128
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,160
and the sound is also quite loud.

129
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,560
By the time I saw him,

130
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,010
it was already too late.

131
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,560
I tried to hit the brakes,

132
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,840
but I think I hit the gas.

133
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:40,960
Calm down.

134
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,490
Try not to get too worked up.

135
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:45,159
What did that person do after that?

136
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,040
Then

137
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,840
he dragged the body over there,

138
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:53,680
cleaned up the scene,

139
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,800
and left.

140
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,360
All right,

141
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:10,800
the scene is cleared.

142
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,760
What should I do now?

143
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:14,880
Should I call an ambulance?

144
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:16,080
No use.

145
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,000
His neck is broken.

146
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,060
He's already dead.

147
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,880
I have other scenes to handle.

148
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:20,680
I'll have my colleagues

149
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,880
come over in a bit.

150
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:31,380
So you weren't the one
who called the police?

151
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:35,039
I waited here for a long time
before you guys showed up.

152
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,080
What's the situation?

153
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:37,960
I just checked.

154
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:40,640
No one was dispatched
to the old thermal power plant tonight.

155
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:41,440
Besides,

156
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:42,450
if someone died,

157
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:44,120
even if another unit passed by

158
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,720
and did the initial handling,

159
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:48,780
they would definitely report it
to the command center.

160
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:51,970
Do you remember
what that person looked like?

161
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,760
He was wearing a mask.

162
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,720
Age...

163
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:58,560
About your age.

164
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:00,980
Then how did you tell
he was a traffic cop?

165
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:04,180
He was wearing a traffic police uniform.

166
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:05,960
Like the ones we're wearing?

167
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:08,640
No.

168
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:11,180
It wasn't a full set like this.

169
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,820
Did he come in a police car?

170
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:17,880
Like our police cars?

171
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:20,280
I don't think so.

172
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:22,480
It was an SUV.

173
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:24,240
A yellow one.

174
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,720
What about the siren lights?

175
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:31,620
I can't remember clearly.

176
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,680
It was a small light.

177
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:37,520
Cylindrical.

178
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:40,010
The kind that sticks to the car.

179
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,040
It's pretty much certain.

180
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,560
You ran into a fake cop.

181
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:43,920
Fake?

182
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:46,400
There are fake traffic cops?

183
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:47,360
Let me tell you,

184
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:47,840
in this day and age,

185
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,100
Jiang, it's really...

186
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:49,940
Get to work.

187
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,240
Ms. Shen,

188
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:53,880
as for this guy,

189
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,960
we'll keep investigating.

190
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:56,880
Don't worry.

191
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:01,490
Do you remember the license plate?

192
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:03,360
I can't remember.

193
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:05,140
The rain was too heavy.

194
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:09,280
Is this a fake cop?

195
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:11,480
More like a real cleaner.

196
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,480
He cleaned it up way too well.

197
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,920
Which way did he go?

198
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:17,680
That way?

199
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:20,680
This way.

200
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:23,000
He made a U-turn and went back.

201
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,130
Going the wrong way?

202
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:33,240
Captain Li, look.

203
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:34,440
It should be this car.

204
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:37,180
How old are these cameras?

205
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,040
They still haven't updated them.

206
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:40,520
The resolution is terrible.

207
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:41,200
Yeah.

208
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,880
The cameras in this area

209
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,040
were installed by the power plant

210
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,160
years ago.

211
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:47,360
Show it to our tech guys

212
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,720
and see if they can restore it.

213
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,400
Okay.

214
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:58,840
Hello, what's up, Chief Zheng?

215
00:10:59,080 --> 00:10:59,760
Captain Li.

216
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:01,810
We've finished up at the scene.

217
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:03,780
Do you know how small the world is?

218
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,360
Did you find something new?

219
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:07,090
More than just a new discovery.

220
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,760
Do you know who the deceased is?

221
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:09,480
Who?

222
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:11,600
Gao Yuhai.

223
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:13,440
Who?

224
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:16,880
The boss of Wending Group,

225
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:19,880
Vice Chairman of the Provincial Federation
of Industry and Commerce, Gao Yuhai.

226
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:20,480
And the Gao Yuhai

227
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:23,080
who almost became your father-in-law.

228
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:25,120
You're Gao Yuhai's daughter?

229
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,960
The star entrepreneur?

230
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:29,960
So what?

231
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,240
What's so surprising?

232
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,240
Of course it's surprising.

233
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:35,160
You...

234
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:35,960
you're

235
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:38,840
the most textbook rich kid ever, and I...

236
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,780
We're not a good match, are we?

237
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:45,400
Captain Li,

238
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,520
Yes, I'm here.

239
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:49,880
Your sister-in-law keeps talking about it,

240
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:52,040
saying you even turned down such a wealthy

241
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:52,840
heir.

242
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:55,280
She doesn't know who else
to set you up with.

243
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:56,610
And then this happened.

244
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:59,240
Xingchen, I'm warning you.

245
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,840
The city will definitely take
this matter very seriously.

246
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,680
You need to be mentally prepared.

247
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:04,740
I'm hanging up now.

248
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:19,320
Given Gao Yuhai's special status

249
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,560
and the high public attention,

250
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:22,040
and more importantly,

251
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:23,240
someone impersonated a traffic cop

252
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:26,080
and tampered with a fatal accident scene,

253
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,000
the bureau

254
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,360
has decided

255
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,260
to set up a special task force.

256
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,520
Officer Li Xingchen

257
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:32,520
is hereby appointed

258
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,120
as the head of the task force.

259
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:34,960
Meanwhile...

260
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,760
Call in Weng Wei

261
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:37,720
from the Criminal Investigation Division

262
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,650
to assist with the investigation.

263
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:46,160
As for the other members
of the task force,

264
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:47,890
you can decide for yourselves.

265
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:50,360
Thank you.

266
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,100
No problem.

267
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:55,560
The city has set up a task force

268
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,000
for your father's case.

269
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:58,560
Our captain went to a meeting
at the bureau.

270
00:12:58,560 --> 00:12:59,820
He should be back soon.

271
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:03,520
They even set up a task force.

272
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:05,300
That's very responsible.

273
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,600
Let me introduce you.

274
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:15,400
Officer Li,

275
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:17,370
I didn't expect to see you here.

276
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:20,200
You guys know each other?

277
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:23,040
We went on a blind date half a year ago.

278
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,100
It's a small world.

279
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:24,840
Ms. Gao,

280
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,640
let me introduce you.

281
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,000
This is Weng Wei from the Criminal
Investigation Detachment,

282
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,800
deputy leader of our task force.

283
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,360
Hello.

284
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,620
Have a seat.

285
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,020
You're Ms. Gao, right?

286
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:43,080
I'd like to ask

287
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:44,480
if you know anything about

288
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:46,720
your father's whereabouts on that street

289
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:47,640
last night.

290
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:54,280
Could you elaborate on that?

291
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:58,080
I'm not entirely sure about the details,

292
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,520
but my father goes to pay his respects

293
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:01,120
to my mother every Saturday.

294
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,040
I saw on the news about 105 before,

295
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:06,560
saying your mother...

296
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:07,720
died in childbirth

297
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:08,800
when she had me.

298
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,360
May I ask

299
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,960
how your relationship with your father is?

300
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:16,920
Officer Weng,

301
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,240
are you suspecting me

302
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,720
by asking this?

